The multiplication table for $\mc W$ in the case of a short nilpotent element $f$ is given by Table <<ref:table4>> ($a,b\in\mf g_0^f$, $u,u_1\in\mf g_{-1}$):

\begin {table}[h]

\begin{center} \begin{tabular}{c||c|c}

$\{\cdot\,_\lambda\,\cdot\}_{z,\rho}$ & $b$ & $\psi(u_1)$

\hline \hline $a$ & $[a,b]+(a|b)\lambda$ & $\psi([a,u_1])+z(s|[a,u_1])$

\hline $\psi(u)$ & $\psi([u,b])+z(s|[u,b])$ & eq.<<ref:20130320:eq2b>>

\end{tabular} \end{center} \end{table}

where the $\lambda$-bracket of $\psi(u)$ and $\psi(u_1)$ is

\begin{equation}
\begin{array}{l}
\displaystyle{
\{\psi(u)_\lambda\psi(u_1)\}_{z,\rho}
=\frac12\sum_{k\in J_1}\psi(u\circ u_k)[u_1,u^k]^\sharp
-\frac12\sum_{k\in J_1}\psi(u_1\circ u_k)[u,u^k]^\sharp
}\\
\displaystyle{
+\frac14\sum_{h,k\in J_1}[[e,u_h],[e,u_k]]
[u,u^h]^\sharp[u_1,u^k]^\sharp
-\frac12(\partial+2\lambda)\psi(u\circ u_1)
}\\
\displaystyle{
+\frac14(\partial+2\lambda)\sum_{k\in J_1}[[e,u],[e,u_k]][u_1,u^k]^\sharp
+\frac14\sum_{k\in J_1} [[e,u_1],[e,u_k]] (\partial+\lambda) [u,u^k]^\sharp
}\\
\displaystyle{
-\frac14\left(3\lambda^2+3\lambda\partial+\partial^2\right)[[e,u],[e,u_1]]
+\frac14(e|u\circ u_1)\lambda^3
}\\
\displaystyle{
+\frac12z\left([[e,u],[s,u_1]]^\sharp-[[e,u_1],[s,u]]^\sharp\right)
-(s|u\circ u_1)z\lambda
\,.
}
\end{array}
\end{equation}

The Virasoro element <<ref:virL>> can be expressed in terms of the generators of $\mc W$ as follows:

\begin{equation}
L=\psi(f)+\frac12\sum_{i\in J_0^f}a_ia^i\,,
\end{equation}

and we have the following $\lambda$-brackets of $L$ with the generators of $\mc W$ ($a\in\mf g_0^f$, $u\in\mf g_{-1}$):

\begin{equation}
\begin{array}{l}
\displaystyle{
\vphantom{\Big)}
\{L_\lambda a\}_{z,\rho}=(\partial+\lambda)a
\,,}\\
\displaystyle{
\vphantom{\Big)}
\{L_\lambda \psi(u)\}_{z,\rho}=(\partial+2\lambda)\psi(u)-\frac12(e|u)\lambda^3+z(s|u)\lambda
\,.}
\end{array}
\end{equation}
